<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Demo BoM for roller shutter — size 1000×2300, box 165, AL slat, manual drive.

    All quantity formulas derived from "roller shuters.xlsx":
      - AL Guide 53x22 (703001): 2 × (height - box_mm) / 1000 m
      - Brush Guide 6x6 (730043): guide_m × 2
      - Gasket XMO 60 (1052001): (height - 72) / 1000 m
      - Terminal 51x8 (704005):  (height - 72) / 1000 m
      - Box Standard 165x165 (701001): (width - 10) / 1000 m
      - Axis 40 (723040): (width - 55) / 1000 m  [manual/chain]
      - Axis 60 (723041): (width - 70) / 1000 m  [electric/radio — O-variant via coeff formula]
      - Slat count: ceil((height - box_mm/2) / slat_height_mm)
      - Slat linear m: slat_count × (width - 72) / 1000
      - Security springs: max(2, floor((height - box_mm) / 500) + 1)
      - Caps: = slat_count (1 cap per slat)
      - Rivets 3×8 + 4×10: 10 each (fixed)
      - Taps WT-900: max(6, ceil(guide_m / 0.5))

    slat_height_mm and slat_weight_kg_m2 come from T1 geometry table.
    box_mm is int(box_size) — e.g. box_size="165" → box_mm=165.
-->
